## Implementation Phases

The project builds **strictly bottom-up**, one phase at a time. No phase may be skipped.

| Phase | Goal | Key Deliverables |
|---|---|---|
| **Phase 0** | Project Initialization | Folder structure, `requirements.txt`, `config.py`, README |
| **Phase 1** | Database Layer | SQLAlchemy models, SQLite adapter, factory, seed data |
| **Phase 2** | NLP Engine | MiniLM loader, embeddings, `intents.json`, classifier |
| **Phase 3** | Conversation Manager | Session state, routing, context, follow-up handling |
| **Phase 4** | Business Services | Order, Return, Recommendation, Handoff services |
| **Phase 5** | Streamlit UI | Chat window, sidebar, history, session reset |
| **Phase 6** | Integration | Wire all layers end-to-end |
| **Phase 7** | Testing | Unit, integration, E2E tests |
| **Phase 8** | Final Polish | Response quality, logging, UI improvements, docs |

> Note: Phase numbering differs between documents (see Inconsistencies below).

---

## Testing Strategy

- **Unit**: NLP classification, each service, repository queries
- **Integration**: Conversation Manager ↔ NLP, Services ↔ Repository, Repository ↔ SQLite
- **E2E Scenarios**: 6 complete user journeys (greeting→order, tracking→returns, recommendation flow, shipping, handoff, fallback recovery)
- **Assignment validation**: Orders 111/222/333 must return exact expected responses

